termios - get and set terminal attributes

SYNOPSIS
    #include "termios.h"
    int tcgetattr(int fd, struct termios *attr);
    int tcsetattr(int fd, int action, const struct termios *attr);
    void cfmakeraw(struct termios *attr);
    int isatty(int fd);

DESCRIPTION
    tcgetattr reads the console's attributes. tcsetattr changes them
    from a foreground job. TCSANOW applies changes immediately.
    TCSADRAIN also applies immediately because console writes are
    synchronous. TCSAFLUSH discards unread input as it applies changes.

    The supported input flags are ICRNL (convert carriage return to
    newline) and IXON (recognize flow-control keys). The supported
    local flags are ICANON, ECHO, ISIG and IEXTEN for line editing,
    echo, signal keys and extended editing keys.

    The c_cc array holds control characters. Zero disables a control
    character. With ICANON clear, reads return available bytes after
    at least one arrives. VMIN must be 1 and VTIME must be 0. The
    output and hardware control fields must be zero.

    cfmakeraw adjusts the supplied settings in memory. Use tcsetattr
    to apply them. The console settings are shared across jobs.
    The pager can also request a temporary per-job input mode.

RETURN VALUES
    tcgetattr and tcsetattr return 0 on success or -1 on error.
    isatty returns 1 for a console descriptor and 0 otherwise.

SEE ALSO
    stty(1), ioctl(2), ttyctl(2)
